course: dictionary
lesson: 5103
title: Big words with a small clue
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some long words are built from parts you already know. Inter means between, and national means of a country. So international means between or involving countries. «The International Space Station has had people on board since 2000.» A space station is not owned by just one country, so international fits.
explain: Look at the words around it. «South Africa accused Israel of genocide at the International Court of Justice, the UN's top court.» The court works for many countries, not just one. Test your meaning by swapping it in: "the between-countries court" still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: In sport, an international is a match between national teams. The same idea shows up in other places too. «Many lorises are caught illegally for the pet trade; all lorises are protected by international law.» Here the law covers more than one country, so it is an international rule.
fact: International means between or involving two or more countries.
fact: The word is built from inter (between) and national (of a country).
fact: In sport, an international is a match between national teams, or a player who has played for their country.
fact: «International law» means rules that protect people or animals across countries, such as lorises.
fact: «International Space Station» is a space station that people have been on board since 2000.
exercise: «All lorises are protected by international law.» What does international law mean? | Rules for one school only | *Rules that cover more than one country | Very long laws | Laws about cooking food
exercise: Inter is the first part of international. Which word means between? | Beside | Under | Above | *Between
exercise: In sport, what is an international? | A match played in one town only | A player who never leaves home | *A match between national teams | A type of ball
test: «The case was expected to take years at the International Court of Justice.» What kind of court is this? | A school hall | A court for one town only | *A court for many countries, the UN's top court | A football court
test: Ayesha says international is hard to read. Which clue helps most? | It has ten letters | It starts with the letter I | *Inter means between and national means of a country | Its last letter is l
exam: Which sentence uses international correctly? | *Trade between Kenya and Japan is international trade | I walked to school international | My bedroom is very international | Her shoes were so international
